MASTER BUILD PROMPT — RADIX TALENT MATCH
Production-quality React frontend for the RADIX Talent Match Hackathon
1. Your Role and Mission
Act as a senior frontend architect, React engineer, UI/UX designer, and product designer.
Build a complete, polished, responsive frontend for RADIX Talent Match, a candidate-centric job-readiness and skill-matching platform developed for the RADIX Talent Match Hackathon.
The application must help candidates understand:
- What skills a particular job requires.
- What skills their resume demonstrates.
- How to build a complete professional profile.
- How ready they are for a particular company's hiring expectations.
- How closely they match a specific job description and which skills they are missing.
Important: Build the frontend only. I will develop and integrate all backend APIs, LLM pipelines, authentication services, and database functionality separately.
Do not stop after creating a landing page. Implement the complete frontend application with all five feature modules, their individual screens, interactions, dashboards, navigation, loading states, error states, and realistic mock data.
Read the supplied RADIX_Talent_Match_Hackathon_Brief.pdf before implementation. Follow its terminology, feature requirements, shared data contract, and workflow. Where the brief does not specify a UI detail, make a sensible product-design decision.

